      "side": 1,
      "message": "You probably know this, but the logic could be condensed to just:\n\n /*\n  * Increment the \"sda is low\" counter if there has not been a write since\n  * the last poll and the SDA line is \"still\" low when sampled.\n  */\n if (last_i2cs_read_irq_count \u003d\u003d i2cs_read_irq_count \u0026\u0026\n     !gpio_get_level(GPIO_I2CS_SDA))\n   i2cs_sda_low_count++;\n else\n   i2cs_sda_low_count \u003d 0;\n\n /*\n  * If sda was low for 5 consecutive samples since the last write\n  * transaction was completed, we assume that the I2C bus is stuck\n  * and reset the controller.\n  */",
